## GitHub PR Workflow

When the user confirms the implementation is complete:

```
# Pull Request creation steps:
1. Stage all changes: git add -A
2. Write a conventional commit message:
   feat(TICKET-KEY): <short description>
3. Push to feature branch: git push origin feature/TICKET-KEY-description
4. Use GitHub MCP or gh CLI to create PR:

# PR Template
Title: feat(TICKET-KEY): <description>

## Summary
<!-- What was built and why -->

## Changes
- Added `FeatureService` with CRUD operations
- Added REST endpoint `POST /api/v1/features`
- Added unit tests with 85% coverage

## Testing
- [ ] Unit tests pass (`./mvnw test`)
- [ ] Integration tests pass
- [ ] Manually verified in local environment

## Jira Ticket
<link to Jira ticket>

## Spec Reference
.cursor/specs/<feature-slug>/

## Screenshots (if UI changes)
```

