## Tool Reference & Fallback Strategy

Always try MCP first. If the MCP server is unavailable, fall back to CLI.

```
# Jira / Confluence / Notion — MCP only (no CLI fallback)
- jira_get_issue(key)                     — fetch ticket + AC
- confluence_get_page(pageId)             — read design doc
- notion_get_page(pageId)                 — read design notes
```

### GitHub — MCP preferred, `gh` CLI fallback

| Action | MCP | CLI Fallback |
|--------|-----|--------------|
| Create PR | `github_create_pull_request(owner, repo, title, head, base, body)` | `gh pr create --title "..." --body "..." --base main` |
| Push changes | `github_push_files(branch, files)` | `git add -A && git commit -m "feat(KEY): msg" && git push origin <branch>` |
| View PR | `github_get_pull_request(owner, repo, N)` | `gh pr view N` |

```bash
# Detect GitHub CLI availability
gh --version   # if this fails, MCP is required or ask user to install gh

# Full PR creation flow via CLI fallback
git checkout -b feature/TICKET-KEY-description
git add -A
git commit -m "feat(TICKET-KEY): short description"
git push origin feature/TICKET-KEY-description
gh pr create \
  --title "feat(TICKET-KEY): short description" \
  --body "## Summary\n...\n## Jira\nTICKET-KEY" \
  --base main
```

> See `.cursor/skills/mcp-tools-reference.md` for the full CLI reference.

